    "title": "Man connected to 2021 shooting in Amarillo sentenced - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Angel Oliva ,\n5 hours ago\nAMARILLO, Texas (KAMR/KCIT) — A man connected to a 2021 deadly shooting in Amarillo was sentenced to 25 years in prison.\nCourt records show that James Coy Mireles pleaded guilty to “Murder” in the death of Timothy Wayne McCullough.\n1 arrested on arson charge following grass fires in Tucumcari Tuesday As was previously reported on Myhighplains.com, on July 17, 2021, the Amarillo Police Department responded to a shooting on the 600 block of south Mississippi Street. McCullough, 24, was found with a gunshot to his head and was taken to a local hospital where he died.\nMireles was later arrested following a SWAT situation in Hereford. He was sentenced to 25 years in prison in March.\nFor the latest Amarillo news and regional updates, check with MyHighPlains.com and tune in to KAMR Local 4 News at 5:00, 6:00, and 10:00 p.m. and Fox 14 News at 9:00 p.m. CST.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KAMR - MyHighPlains.com.",
    "summary": "Court records show that James Coy Mireles pleaded guilty to “Murder” in the death of Timothy Wayne McCullough. 1 arrested on arson charge following grass fires in Tucumcari Tuesday As was previously reported on Myhighplains.com, on July 17, 2021, the Amarillo Police Department responded to a shooting on the 600 block of south Mississippi Street. McCullough, 24, was found with a gunshot to his head and was taken to a local hospital where he died. Mireles was later arrested following a SWAT situation in Hereford. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KAMR - MyHighPlains.com.",
